Package: distribumpy
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexy@gmail.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, flatpak, libxkbcommon0, libegl1
Recommends: xdg-utils
Suggests: libvulkan1
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/distribumpy
Description: a Flatpak store in the LineXinBar design language
 Shown as Software Hub. It installs, updates and removes Flatpak applications
 through libflatpak — the same library the flatpak command is a front end for
 — so a transaction here is the transaction that command would have run:
 resolved dependencies, progress operation by operation, and a cancel that
 works.
 .
 It reads the AppStream catalogue every remote already keeps on the disk, so a
 machine that has been updated once can be browsed with the network unplugged.
 New applications are installed for the current user by default, which needs no
 password; anything already installed for the whole system is listed, updated
 and removed as readily.
 .
 It is an ordinary Wayland application, drawn in the LineXinBar design language
 and driven from a keyboard, a pointer, a touchscreen and a controller at once.
 It runs under GNOME or Plasma as readily as under the shell it was made for.
 .
 libxkbcommon0 and libegl1 are named here because they are opened by name at
 run time rather than linked, so nothing that reads the executable can find
 them. libvulkan1 is only suggested: with a Vulkan driver present this draws
 through it, and without one it falls back to EGL.
